
page trace in AlphaByNod


type trace -- instrisic,restricted
{{	
	A trace is a source code locator.

	Type trace is restricted.  It can't be created, sub-
	typed, or used in another type instance. 

	Trace objects are created when an application quits. If
	an application specifies an object definition in the
	quit expression (using "with"), the HNM creates the
	object and attaches it to the trace object along with
	location info. 

	If a trace doesn't have an object, :use_object returns
	a void proxy.

	Note: See alpha\fault for an example quit object type.
	Alpha disruptions always quit with a fault object.

	location is a formatted expr that includes book name,
	page name, and line number.  Currently, the precise
	format is undefined.

	A trace object can be accessed via a disruption proxy
	named ~disruption that is only visible in a trap block.
	See alpha\disruption for details.

}}
{
	general 
	{
		use_location = expr prox [eval];

		get_location ()( expr );

		use_object = object prox [eval]; -- may be void
	}
}

